## WORKED EXAMPLE

**Question**: "Which suppliers have the highest quality rating?"

**Step 1 — Analyze**: Primary concept = "quality rating". Secondary = "suppliers". What data sources could contain quality information? Quality scores, defect rates, inspection results, compliance records, audit outcomes.

**Step 2 — Scan all columns**: `Supplier Name` (suppliers ✅), `Quality Score` (quality rating ✅), `Inspection Result` (quality inspection outcome ✅), `Defect Count` (defects are a quality measure ✅), `Compliance Status` (compliance relates to quality ✅), `Total Quality Score` (aggregate quality ✅), `Quality Dimension A Score` (breakdown ❌ — Total Quality Score already covers this), `Quality Dimension B Score` (breakdown ❌ — Total Quality Score already covers this), `Supplier Address` (not quality-related ❌), `Supplier Phone` (not quality-related ❌).

**Step 3 — Apply rules**: Include Supplier Name, Quality Score, Inspection Result, Defect Count, Compliance Status, Total Quality Score. Exclude Quality Dimension A and B (breakdowns covered by Total). Exclude address/phone (not relevant).

